   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024 the Australia-Fiji Education Program supported Fiji&#x2019;s Ministry of Education to revise and pilot a new literacy and numeracy  curriculum across 90 primary schools. This has resulted in significant improvements in student reading, writing, and numeracy compared to 10 control schools. Notably, three special education schools involved in the trials showed marked gains in literacy, affirming the curriculum&#x2019;s inclusivity. To further enhance learning outcomes, the program piloted 20 community learning spaces (CLS), which lifted  homework completion rates to over 90% and increased student engagement, prompting additional communities to self-fund CLS initiatives. This success has led the Ministry for I-Taukei Affairs to expand the model to 112 communities. Additionally, the program supported 98 remote, rural, and maritime &#x201c;Hope Schools&#x201d; (less than 50% pass rate in Year 8) to receive library resources, and within two years, 97 of them improved sufficiently to no longer be classified as such.</narrative>
    </description>
